# Gitignored files copied into each worktree Claude Code creates.
#
# Uses .gitignore syntax. Only files that match a pattern AND are gitignored are
# copied, so nothing tracked is ever duplicated. Applies to worktrees created by
# `--worktree`, by subagent isolation, and by the desktop app; a WorktreeCreate
# hook replaces the mechanism entirely and must copy these itself.
#
# This covers only the file half of setting up a worktree. It cannot install
# dependencies, and it cannot reach the Claude project memory, which lives
# outside the repository — run `node scripts/claude/setup-worktree.mjs` for
# those. See .ai/WORKTREES.md.

# Docs site secrets. Absent from a fresh worktree, so docs work and the docs
# test suite fail there with no explanation.
docs/.env
docs/tests/.env

# Deliberately NOT copied — listing these here would cause real bugs:
#
#   node_modules            A copy is not an install. Per-package `.bin` shims
#                           would still be missing and package scripts still die
#                           with exit 127.
#   handsontable/dist       Build outputs. A stale copy is exactly the
#   handsontable/tmp        "silently testing the wrong build" failure this
#   handsontable/styles     repository already has to guard against elsewhere.
#   .code-review-graph/     Branch-stamped. A copy answers cross-file queries
#                           with another branch's structure, which is worse than
#                           having no graph at all.
#   .claude/settings.local.json
#                           Not needed. Since Claude Code v2.1.211 a permission
#                           approval made in a worktree is saved to the MAIN
#                           checkout's file and applies in every worktree of the
#                           repository, so a copy here would only go stale.
